<title>IRAN: Iran in copper deal with Japanese, Australian firm.</title>
<headline>Iran in copper deal with Japanese, Australian firm.</headline>
<dateline>TEHRAN 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran has signed a contract with three international companies to develop copper smelting works at the Islamic republic's Sarcheshmeh mine, the official Iranian news agency IRNA said.</p>
<p>It quoted Minister of Mines and Metals Mohammad Hossein Mahlouji as saying that his ministry had signed a contract with Tomen Corp of Japan and Broken Hill Proprietary Co and MIM Holdings of Australia.</p>
<p>The deal involves doubling the annual capacity at Sarcheshmeh to 200,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>IRNA did not say when the deal was signed or when work would begin.</p>
<p>In January Iran's parliament authorised the government to use $400 million in the Iranian year to March 1998 to increase copper production.</p>
</text>
